# LCV-172 AC 7, LCV-177 AC 1 — a cubic Bézier imports as a cubic entity and
# moves the current point to its endpoint. LCV-176 AC 1 — the elliptical arc
# (rx 20 != ry 10) imports as an elliptical arc. World y = 100 - svg y.
bed 100 100
# LCV-175: every stroke is red and no layer is declared, so one `#ff0000` layer.
layer "#ff0000" #ff0000 output=1 current=1
# M 10 10 C 20 0 30 20 40 10, mirrored.
cubic 0 10 90 20 100 30 80 40 90
# After C, the current point is (40, 10); L 40 30.
line 0 40 90 40 70
# A 20 10 0 0 1 80 30 from (40, 30): the chord is the major axis (lambda = 1),
# so the centre is (60, 30) and the arc is the half above it on screen (sweep
# 1 = clockwise in SVG), user parameter pi -> 2pi. The Y mirror reflects it:
# world centre (60, 70), parameter -180 -> 0 degrees, clockwise.
ellipse 0 60 70 20 10 0 -180 0 cw
# After A, the current point is (80, 30); L 80 50.
line 0 80 70 80 50
